   "kind": "published",
   "source": "SPEC",
   "note": "MTOW 15,000 lb, max ramp 15,100 lb, MZFW 12,500 lb, MLW 15,000 lb."
  },
  {
   "field": "mass.empty_kg",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "SPEC",
   "note": "Basic empty weight ~9,300 lb including unusable fuel and oil (typical delivered 350s are 9,100-9,500 lb); a basic operating weight is ~9,955 lb with a crew of two."
  },
  {
   "field": "mass.empty_cg_m, mass.cg_forward_limit, mass.cg_aft_limit",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "Empty CG and an envelope of about 17-35 % MAC; the published envelope (inches aft of the B300 datum) is not transcribed."
  },
  {
   "field": "mass.empty_inertia_kgm2",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "ROSKAM",
   "note": "Twin-turboprop radii of gyration Rx 0.34, Ry 0.29, Rz 0.44 on the empty mass (the wing fuel and payload add theirs)."
  },
  {
   "field": "surfaces[0]",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "NACA",
   "note": "Planform matching the published area and span: centre section 2.15/2.0 m chord to the nacelles (2.9 m), outer panel 2.0/0.92 m with 2 deg of quarter-chord sweep, 6 deg dihedral, 0.6 m winglets canted 72 deg; incidence 2.5 deg root to -1 deg tip (3.5 deg of washout as the King Air family's ~3.8 deg root / ~0 deg tip, set 1 deg lower for the attitudes with flap). NACA 230-series section: clmax 1.62 at flight Reynolds numbers (~8e6), cm0 -0.01. Slipstream exposure 0.8 on the strips behind the propellers."
  },
  {
   "field": "surfaces[0].panels[*].controls.flap",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "Single-slotted flaps inboard and outboard of the nacelles to ~55 % semi-span, 30 % chord, approach 14 deg and down 35 deg (published as 'approach' and 'full', angles estimated), chord extension 10 %, dclmax/dcl 0.9: landing CLmax ~2.1, the class of the published landing-configuration stall (VSO ~81 KIAS at MTOW, the B200's 76 KIAS at 12,500 lb on a similar wing)."
  },
  {
   "field": "surfaces[1], surfaces[2]",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "T-tail from photographs and three-views: tailplane 5.6 m span, 1.2/0.62 m chords (5.2 m^2), 14 deg sweep, 2.6 m above the fuselage centreline (clear of the slipstream), incidence -1.5 deg; swept fin 2.05 m tall, 2.7/1.25 m chords. Tail volume ~0.8."
  },
  {
   "field": "fuselages, drag_items",
   "kind": "calibrated",
   "source": "ROSKAM",
   "note": "Flat-plate areas from a wetted-area build-up (fuselage 0.21, nacelles and exhaust stacks 0.13, excrescences, antennas, cooling inlets and interference 0.09 m^2 of CdA); with the strips' profile drag CD0 ~0.025. The excrescence item is the one adjusted against the published maximum cruise speed."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops",
   "kind": "published",
   "source": "ENG",
   "note": "PT6A-60A: 1,050 shp flat-rated (take-off and maximum continuous) at 1,700 rpm, i.e. 100 % torque = 4,398 N m (3,244 ft lbf) at the propeller shaft; SFC 0.548 lb/shp/h; ITT limit 820 degC; Ng 100 % = 37,468 rpm, limit 104 %. Two engines, both turning clockwise seen from behind (no counter-rotation: the left engine is critical)."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops[*].thermodynamic_power_shp, itt_theta_exponent, gas_power_exponent, ng_zero_power",
   "kind": "calibrated",
   "source": "SARAVANAMUTTOO",
   "note": "Gas power on corrected parameters (delta0 sqrt(theta0) x g(Ng/sqrt(theta0)), g cubic from 50 % Ng) with the ITT limit reached at 100 % corrected Ng at sea level ISA: a thermodynamic rating of 1,575 shp (1.5 x the flat rating) and ITT = theta0^0.15 x the corrected ITT put the end of the flat rating (torque limit to ITT limit) near 15,000 ft ISA in the climb and ~780 shp at FL240 at 300 KTAS, the power class of the published maximum cruise. Take-off at sea level ISA: Ng ~94 %, ITT ~770 degC, torque-limited; still torque-limited at ISA+20."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops[*].ng_low_idle, ng_high_idle, itt_idle_c, idle_fuel_flow_lb_per_h, acceleration_time_s, start_time_s, light_off_ng",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "PT6 class: low idle 62 % Ng, high idle 72 %, idle ITT ~600 degC, idle fuel ~100 lb/h; light-off at 13 % Ng with the starter (the starter alone turns ~22 %), self-sustaining from ~45 %, ~30 s to stabilised idle; Ng spools 95 % of a step in 5 s up, 3 s down. Starter-generators 300 A, on line from 50 % Ng."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops[*].turbine_stall_torque_ratio, inertia_kgm2, friction_torque_fraction",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "SARAVANAMUTTOO",
   "note": "Free power turbine: torque falls linearly with Np from 2x the design torque at rest (the usual free-turbine characteristic). Power turbine and reduction gearbox referred to the propeller shaft 6 kg m^2, plus the propeller's 24 kg m^2 (four aluminium blades ~13 kg each); gearbox drag 1 % of the rated torque at rated Np."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops[*].governor, reverse, autofeather",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "Hydraulic constant-speed governor: blade-angle rate 5 deg/s per 1 % Np error with a 0.15 s lead, 15 deg/s pitch rate, feathering by spring and counterweights at 8 deg/s; governor oil from 40 % Np (the propeller feathers as the engine runs down on the ground, but a windmilling propeller keeps its oil in flight). Beta over the first 40 % of the reverse travel (flight-idle stop to -10 deg at idle Ng), reverse Ng to 85 % with Np held to 95 %. Autofeather armed with the power levers above 85 % travel and both torques above 24 %, feathering an engine whose torque falls below 12 % (the King Air 350's system arms near 90 % N1 and trips near 400 ft lbf, ~12 %)."
  },
  {
   "field": "turboprops[*].propeller",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "TCDS",
   "note": "Hartzell four-blade, 105 in (2.67 m), 1,700 rpm (published). Blade planform (max chord 0.21 m at mid-span, activity factor ~110), thickness and section estimated. Blade angles at 0.75 R: reverse -10 deg, flight-idle low-pitch stop 14 deg, feather 86 deg (Estimated); governed range 1,450-1,700 rpm. Static take-off thrust from the BEM ~13 kN per engine at 100 % torque."
  },
  {
   "field": "fuel",
   "kind": "published",
   "source": "SPEC",
   "note": "539 US gal (2,040 l) usable in two wing systems (nacelle and wing tanks per side, lumped); Jet A 0.80 kg/l; unusable ~3 US gal per side (Estimated)."
  },
  {
   "field": "gear",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "EST",
   "note": "Tricycle: twin-wheel mains (22 x 6.75-10, 105 psi) retracting into the nacelles, track 5.23 m (published), single steerable nose wheel 4.9 m ahead (wheelbase estimated). Oleo struts sized for ~0.1 m static deflection and 0.4 critical damping at MTOW; brakes 4 kN m per main (~0.4 g at MTOW), no anti-skid. Nose-wheel steering by the pedals +-14 deg. Electro-hydraulic gear, 6 s transit."
  },
  {
   "field": "controls",
   "kind": "estimated",
   "source": "TCDS",
   "note": "Flap detents up / approach / down; electric flaps ~12 s full travel; elevator trim tab range 12 deg; rudder boost not modelled. Yaw damper (fitted): washed-out yaw rate to the rudder, 25 % authority."
  },
  {
   "field": "limits",
   "kind": "published",
   "source": "TCDS",
   "note": "Vmo 263 KIAS, Mmo 0.58; VFE 202 KIAS (approach) / 158 KIAS (down); VLE 184 KIAS; VA ~182 KIAS; load factors +3.17 / -1.27 g (flaps up), +2.0 g flaps down (normal-category figures; Estimated for the commuter certification basis)."
  },
  {
   "field": "stall_warning",
